#### Comparison of Data with Results from Model Calculations

We compare experimental results of photon multiplicity fluctuations with HIJING and participant model. The results are calculated with very fine centrality bins, i.e., 2% centrality bins. Fig. 5.23 clearly shows that relative photon multiplicity fluctuations, \(\omega_{\gamma}\) in data are more or less constant within the statistical error bars, with a value of \(\sim\) 7. Whereas, HIJING model calculations show slightly large relative photon multiplicity fluctuations with a value of \(\sim\) 8. A comparison of data and HIJING values is also made with participant model in this figure. Relative fluctuations in this model gradually rise from a value of \(\sim\) 2 and remain constant for the rest of the centrality, with a value of \(\sim\) 3. Fig. 5.23 also shows that the participant model clearly fails to explain the observed photon multiplicity fluctuations in \(Cu+Cu\) collisions. The error bars shown here are statistical only.

